<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  {{> head}}
  <body id="compare-page" class="bg-white text-slate-900 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-slate-100 antialiased">
    {{> header}}
    <div class="doc-layout mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8">
      <main class="doc-main min-w-0">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-1">
        <a href="/{{left.id}}" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">{{left.id}}</a>
        <span class="text-slate-400">↔</span>
        <a href="/{{right.id}}" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">{{right.id}}</a>
      </h1>
      <p class="compare-note mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        Resources are paired by their export path, which is a heuristic: two tenants can hold different policies under
        the same name, and a renamed policy shows once on each side. Listed from each export's
        <code class="font-mono">resources/metadata.yaml</code>, resources still present in the tenant only; a pair's
        status compares the two files after the provisional normalisation. Types the documentation leaves out come last.
      </p>

      {{> compare_pane pane leftId=left.id rightId=right.id}}

      <div class="compare-diff-area rounded-lg border border-dashed border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700 px-4 py-6 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        {{#if pane.firstDifferenceHref}}
          Select a pair above to see its diff, or <a href="{{pane.firstDifferenceHref}}" class="compare-first-difference text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">open the first difference</a>.
        {{else}}
          Select a pair above to see its diff. No pair differs.
        {{/if}}
      </div>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
